const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"把一个持有期放回一生",en:"Put one holding period into lifetime choice"},body:{zh:"Merton把消费与投资放进持续决策的问题。今天的资产选择不仅影响下一期财富，也影响以后能怎样消费和配置资产。因此，单期均值与方差的比较，未必完整描述一个面向长期的投资者所关心的风险。",en:"Merton embeds consumption and investment in continuing choice. Today's holdings affect both next-period wealth and later opportunities to consume and invest. A one-period mean–variance comparison need not capture every risk relevant to a lifetime decision."},reference:{url:"https://breesefine7110.tulane.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/16/2015/10/Merton-Int.-CAPM.pdf",label:{zh:"1973年期刊版 · pp. 867–868",en:"1973 journal article · pp. 867–868"}}},{title:{zh:"机会集本身也会变化",en:"The opportunity set can itself change"},body:{zh:"未来可获得的收益分布并不一定保持不变。投资者除了关心财富涨跌，还可能在意利率或其他投资条件的变化。理解跨期风险，要把资产本身的当期收益与未来可投资机会的状态分开，而非只增加一个预测期限。",en:"Future return distributions need not stay fixed. Investors can care about changing investment conditions as well as changing wealth. Intertemporal risk therefore separates current asset returns from the state of future opportunities, rather than merely extending a forecast horizon."},reference:{url:"https://breesefine7110.tulane.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/16/2015/10/Merton-Int.-CAPM.pdf",label:{zh:"1973年期刊版 · p. 869",en:"1973 journal article · p. 869"}}},{title:{zh:"共同预期仍然是一项假设",en:"Common expectations remain an assumption"},body:{zh:"从单期转向跨期，并不意味着论文同时解决了所有市场摩擦。作者仍保留共同预期、价格接受者与市场出清等条件。比较模型时，应识别究竟放松了哪一项假设，不能把动态结构误读成对现实复杂性的全面覆盖。",en:"Moving to multiple periods does not resolve every friction. Common expectations, price taking and market clearing remain assumptions. Model comparisons should identify the particular restriction being relaxed; a dynamic structure is not comprehensive realism."},reference:{url:"https://breesefine7110.tulane.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/16/2015/10/Merton-Int.-CAPM.pdf",label:{zh:"1973年期刊版 · pp. 868–869",en:"1973 journal article · pp. 868–869"}}},{title:{zh:"融资与交易条件先于推论",en:"Financing assumptions precede conclusions"},body:{zh:"模型允许连续交易、资产可分割和卖空，并采用相同的借贷利率，同时忽略税费及交易成本。这些条件帮助建立理论关系，却与有交易时段、融资额度或借券限制的账户不同，不能将理论可行组合直接视为可实施方案。",en:"Continuous trading, divisibility, short selling and common lending and borrowing rates simplify the argument. Taxes and transaction costs are absent. The feasible set differs from an account with trading hours, credit limits or restricted stock borrowing."},reference:{url:"https://breesefine7110.tulane.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/16/2015/10/Merton-Int.-CAPM.pdf",label:{zh:"1973年期刊版 · p. 868",en:"1973 journal article · p. 868"}}},{title:{zh:"资产总价值不等于每股价格",en:"Total asset value differs from a share price"},body:{zh:"讨论资产供给时，论文区分资产产生消费品的能力与所有权份额的价格。新增投资、折旧或发行会改变总资产及份额数量。观察公司总价值的变化时，不能省略股数变化而直接解释成现有每股持有者的收益。",en:"The supply discussion separates productive assets from ownership shares. Investment, depreciation or issuance can alter asset totals and share counts. A change in aggregate firm value cannot be read as an existing shareholder's return without accounting for those quantities."},reference:{url:"https://breesefine7110.tulane.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/16/2015/10/Merton-Int.-CAPM.pdf",label:{zh:"1973年期刊版 · p. 870",en:"1973 journal article · p. 870"}}},{title:{zh:"跨期框架提出更具体的问题",en:"The framework sharpens the question"},body:{zh:"阅读这篇文章的价值，是重新问清楚什么状态对未来消费不利，以及哪些资产与这些状态共同变化。它并没有仅凭历史价格就提供答案；从理论状态到可观测变量，还需要另外建立测量、样本和经验检验之间的联系。",en:"The framework asks which states harm future consumption and which assets move with them. Historical prices alone do not answer that question. Connecting theoretical states to observations requires separate measurement choices, sample definitions and empirical tests."},reference:{url:"https://breesefine7110.tulane.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/16/2015/10/Merton-Int.-CAPM.pdf",label:{zh:"1973年期刊版 · pp. 867–870",en:"1973 journal article · pp. 867–870"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"这是连续时间均衡理论，不是当前市场的估计模型。无交易成本、相同借贷利率和可卖空等假设，不能直接当作现实账户条件。",en:"This is continuous-time equilibrium theory, not a fitted model of today's market. Frictionless trading, common borrowing rates and short selling are assumptions, not account capabilities."}};export{e as default};
